<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bodhisattva</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as bodhisattvas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A bodhisattva, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, is a being who has attained great spiritual merit and seeks enlightenment for the benefit of all, a central ideal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahayana-buddhism">Mahayana Buddhism</a>. In Gandharan art, which grew from the Greek culture left by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>, Greek sculptural style was adapted to depict the Buddha and bodhisattvas. This visual tradition later spread across Central and East Asian Buddhism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bodhisattva.jpg" alt="Bodhisattva" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plaosan_Bodhisattva_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
